<title>USA: LPC - Celulosa taps Morgan for $300 mln bank loan.</title>
<headline>LPC - Celulosa taps Morgan for $300 mln bank loan.</headline>
<text>
<p>NEW YORK, Oct 28 (LPC) - J.P. Morgan &amp; Co Inc is leading a $300 million bank loan backing Chilean pulp and paper company Celulosa Arauco's roughly $430 million acquisition of Argentine pulp concern Alto Parana, according to banking sources.</p>
<p>The credit has set a benchmark low in pricing for BBB rated Chilean borrowers, banking sources said.</p>
<p>At the company's current rating, starting pricing is 35 basis points over the London Inter-Bank Offered Rate (LIBOR), a banker said.</p>
<p>Pricing can fall as low as 27 basis points over LIBOR or rise as high as 55 basis points over LIBOR, depending on Celulosa's rating, the banker added.</p>
<p>-- Meredith Coffey, LPC Editorial, 212 489-5455</p>
